<title>FRANCE: ADP export traffic down 0.2pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>ADP export traffic down 0.2pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air cargo exports totalling 588,665 tonnes of left the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in 1996, down 0.2 percent on 1995, airport authority figures show.</p>
<p>Global 1996 export traffic from the ADP, by region, with percentage change on 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p>			     1996 tonnage	   change from 1995</p>
<p> Domestic		  46,787 tonnes	 up    0.7pct</p>
<p> European Union	  69,379 tonnes	 up    4.6</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	   13,321 tonnes     down    0.1</p>
<p> North Africa	    10,522 tonnes     down   29.1</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa    48,459 tonnes	 up    1.9</p>
<p> North America	  161,835 tonnes	 up    0.2</p>
<p> French territories    27,450 tonnes     down    3.2</p>
<p> Latin America	   31,106 tonnes	 up    2.9</p>
<p> Middle East	     58,089 tonnes	 up    7.3</p>
<p> Far East		 121,716 tonnes     down    4.2</p>
<p> Total		    588,665 tonnes     down    0.2</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
